# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks every file out as
# CRLF. That is invisible for most files, but it silently breaks two things:
#
#   1. entrypoint.sh gets copied into the Docker image with CRLF, so the shebang
#      reads "#!/bin/sh\r" and the container dies with
#      "exec /entrypoint.sh failed: No such file or directory".
#   2. Prettier flags every file in the frontend, because it expects LF, which
#      buries any real formatting problem in ~900 false positives.
#
# The repository already stores LF, so this changes no committed content - it
# only makes checkouts consistent across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts and container inputs must be LF even if the rule above is relaxed.
*.sh        text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp3  binary
*.flac binary
*.opus binary
*.aac  binary
*.wma  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.wav  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
